(i) we propose a two-branch network mapping forgery artifacts from paired original and compressed forgeries to a compression-insensitive embedding feature space by using an adversarial-learning strategy;
(ii) we propose a metric loss function that reduces the distance of the paired images of two different compression levels in the embedding feature space, which further encourages the network to extract the compression-insensitive features.

